WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your girls are 4 and 2?
-They are 4 and 2.

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.770
-And, now, I'm assuming
they're not gonna see this film,

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.738 line:92%
but have they seen you on film?

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:06.206 size:78% position:39%
And how do they react
when they see you?

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:09.709
-My daughters, in general,
loathe to see me on-screen.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:12.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-In general, you know?

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know, when I was
doing "Mary Poppins,"

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd even FaceTime my daughter,
and she'd be like,

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:20.553 size:81% position:41%
"Take that silly old
Mary Poppins wig off."

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:23.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was like,
"I like your blond hair."

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:24.524 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's lovely.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:27.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But, actually, we were having
a Super Bowl Party,

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:30.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the trailer for
"Quiet Place" came on,

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:31.898 size:75% position:38% line:92%
which is terrifying.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:32.332 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Hazel sort of wandered in
with a hot dog in hand.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:39.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she goes like this --
She goes, "Whoa."

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.673 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's you, Mommy."

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:41.608 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And I was like, "Yeah."

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then there was
a bit where I scream.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if
anyone's seen the trailer,

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:47.047
but I'm literally like [screams]
at the end of the trailer.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:49.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she -- You could see
her brain exploding.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:53.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, instead,
she went, "Ha...cool."

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.190
And then, like, walked out
and never talked about it again.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:59.526 size:78% position:39%
-Well, that's the key
to parenting is --

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:00.560 line:92%
when a traumatic thing happens,

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
just let them
deal on it on their own.

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Listen, that's how
I was raised.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:05.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's like the British way.
-That's the British way.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:08.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
They know something
painful's happened to you.

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:08.835 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Give it 10 years.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sweep it under the carpet.
Yeah.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.873
-Are you -- You must be excited
for them to see "Mary Poppins."

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.943
-Well, they are in love with
Julie Andrews' Mary Poppins.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. And had they
been in love --

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I guess they're not
old enough to have been

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:22.582
in love with it for a long time,
but how long have they seen --

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:25.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I never
showed it to them

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.587 line:92%
during my shooting of the film,

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:31.124
partly 'cause I just selfishly
didn't want to be so distracted

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
by how brilliant Julie Andrews
was in the role,

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:36.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
already feeling that there was
this, like, iconic boulder

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:39.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I had to, like,
move aside to play this part.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.534
-Were you worried that, like,
your kids will see this one

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:44.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
and be like, "You're our
second-favorite Mary Poppins"?

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:46.473 line:92%
-Oh, I'm not even on the list.

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.374 line:92%
They're, like, creepy obsessed

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:49.876 line:92%
with Julie Andrews now, yeah.

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:52.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That will be a terrifying
moment, then, for you.

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:53.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
That will be scarier than
"A Quiet Place,"

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:54.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
having to watch
your kids react to it.

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.917
-Yeah, I just don't even think
they should see "Mary Poppins."

00:01:57.917 --> 00:01:59.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, they should
never watch it.

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:02.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This will be your third film
with Meryl Streep.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:04.457
-I know.
It's like, "Get your own movie."

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:05.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what I mean?
-Exactly.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:10.530
Thank you for saying that,
'cause I thought the same thing.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.265 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Stalker.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:15.401
Yeah, and we always play people
who sort of loathe each other

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:16.302 size:88% position:44% line:92%
in the films that we do.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:19.706
-Is there truth to the rumor
"The Devil Wears Prada" --

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:21.641 size:81% position:41%
There might be another
"Devil Wears Prada"?

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:24.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, I would love it.
-Yeah.

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:27.080 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.081 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We all would.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:30.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you know Stanley Tucci
is my brother-in-law?

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did know that Stanley Tucci
was your Brother-in-Law.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He, like, wormed
his way into the family.

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:36.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But he wasn't during
the first "Devil Wears --"

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. So, we met on
the first movie.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:40.660 size:84% position:42%
I'm talking about like
there is another movie.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
We met on the
first "Devil Wears Prada."

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:46.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just loved him so much,
so he was at our wedding

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:48.234 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and then met my sister.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's unbelievable.
-I know.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.470
-And they've been married
for a while now, right?

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.305
-They've been married --
I don't even know how long.

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:53.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Too long.
-Too long. Yeah.

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:58.378
And when you met John, he was
already on "The Office," yes?

00:02:58.378 --> 00:02:58.945 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-He was, yeah.

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:01.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And were you aware of
that show when you met him?

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:04.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was sort of aware that
he was vaguely recognizable,

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:04.717 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but I was a huge --

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:07.554 size:78% position:39%
-That's so romantic.
-Yeah. It was like...

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:09.055 line:92%
"You look blurily familiar."

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:12.792
Yeah. But I was a big fan
of the British "Office."

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:13.226 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh.

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:16.062
That's what the people on the
American "Office" love to hear.

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:17.564 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:19.065 line:92%
And then I sort of binge-watched

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:21.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
the American "Office"
and loved it.

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:23.269 line:92%
-And how did you guys meet?

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:25.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's, like,
kind of a sad, lame story.

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:27.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, not sad,
but it's just kind of lame.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:30.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I was in a restaurant.
He was in the restaurant.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was sitting with
a mutual friend.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:35.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is our romantic comedy.
This is it. Write it!

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:36.716 line:92%
-This is Paul and Meredith.

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:39.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And my friend Gray goes,
"Oh, my God.

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:41.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's my friend John."
And that was it.

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:43.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:43.923 line:92%
-And he came over to the table?

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:46.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Guys, it's golden.
It's cinema gold.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:46.893 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It is really good.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:49.529
Did he -- I'm sorry to ask
for the logistics to this.

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:51.464
Did he then come over and
eat his meal with you?

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:55.668
-No. He was actually sitting
with our friend Justin Theroux.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:56.336 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:57.637 line:92%
-And then he abandoned Justin

00:03:57.637 --> 00:04:01.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
and came over to come
and talk to us.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:01.741 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He did not eat.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:04.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
He just stood there
and made me laugh. Yeah.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
And it's worked out.

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:06.679 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-He just did a bit.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:09.415
-And all these years later...
And did you know right away?

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:11.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sorry to dig in here.
-I kind of did.

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:12.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:16.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's good.
-Am I speaking to "Us Weekly"?

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:16.756 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I love you. I'm sorry.

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:20.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just want to make it clear
that you guys, as stars,

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.261 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
are just like us.

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:24.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
I am just like you guys.

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
-But I'm so happy.

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:27.667
-It really is -- I mean,
for waiting to see you guys

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
work together, I never would
have predicted this film.

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it just so wonderful
that you guys did it.

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:32.071 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-It's so disturbing.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:34.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's really disturbing,
but it's really great.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's so good.
I'm thrilled you love it.

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:37.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's sort of been
overwhelming, actually,

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:40.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause we were really nervous
to work together,

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
and terrified --
John, in general,

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:45.652
was sort of terrified of, like,
how people will view this film

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:46.519 line:92%
or whether they'll accept it.

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
And people have just been
incredible about it.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:51.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
They just love it.
-Well, they're right.

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:52.525 size:81% position:41% line:92%
It's really wonderful.

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:54.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
And thank you so much
for being here.

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:56.362
It's just a delight to have you.
-Hey, anytime.

